## ui_component_refactor_plan

### Current Progress
- **Phase 1: Align with page model** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 2: Section metadata** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 3: Integration primitives** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 4: Component registry & bind-point contracts** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 5: Open derived/custom sections to registered components** - 🟡 In progress
- **Phase 6: Convert routes to dynamic page rendering** - ⬜ Not started
- **Phase 7: Document compatibility hardening** - ✅ Complete

### Phase 5 Progress
- [x] Component picker UI in `DerivedSectionBlock` and `CustomSectionBlock` (2026-06-09)
- [x] Bind-point mapping UI (column => bind-point) with `ComponentBindMapper` (2026-06-09)
- [x] Component-driven row rendering with `ComponentGrid` (2026-06-09)
- [x] `DesignedCardWrapper` added for card-level style composition (2026-06-11)
- [x] `ComponentGroupEditor` refactored with tab UI (layout/styles) and `CardDesigner` integration (2026-06-11)
- [x] `ComponentRenderer` extended with `MediaScraperCard` compound component (2026-06-11)
- [x] CSS sanitization added to `DesignedCardWrapper` for safe `customCss` rendering (2026-06-11)
- [x] Shared section compatibility matrix, sanitized production-shape fixtures,
      and 19-type registry drift tests retained by `custom_page_document_model_consolidation`
      (2026-07-17)
- [x] All page-section renderer families now use the shared `SectionFrame`, one
      toolbar with type-specific action portals, and the exhaustive renderer
      registry (2026-07-17)
- [x] `custom_page_document_model_consolidation` retained these useful registry
      and shared-UI pieces while retiring the unused typed persistence/API
      experiment (2026-08-16)

### Next Steps
- [ ] Continue Phase 5: add component group rendering/editing to remaining section types.
- [ ] Add focused tests for component-rendered section behavior when the frontend test harness is normalized.
- [ ] Verify refactored UI components as part of `.todo/live_testing`.
- [ ] Coordinate with `.todo/custom_page_document_model_consolidation`: reuse the
      slim JSON-native section/component registries and shared document UI; do
